1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,956
A college senior hoped for a thousand GitHub stars.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,943
His next one got 83,000.

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:06,400
And a billionaire's backing.

4
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,103
For this.

5
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:08,362
He built MiroFish.

6
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:11,495
It simulates thousands of people, to predict the future.

7
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,067
Step one. Feed it anything.

8
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,012
It maps every person and connection.

9
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,898
Then turns each one into an AI agent.

10
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:19,080
Thousands of them, arguing, changing minds.

11
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,099
Basically, the internet. In a box.

12
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,030
Two fake social networks, at once.

13
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:24,885
Then you play god, and drop in a what-if.

14
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,861
It writes you a prediction report.

15
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,795
And you can interview the agents.

16
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,400
Then: a centuries-old novel.

17
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:33,056
The author never finished it. So the characters did.

18
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:33,640
The catch?

19
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:35,030
Their homepage: five bucks a run.

20
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:36,099
README: go easy.

21
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:37,250
Futures from five bucks.

22
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:38,600
It can't see the future.

23
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:40,384
It rehearses a thousand of them.

24
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,763
So we asked a swarm about this video.

25
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,000
73% say you'll follow.

26
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:47,053
Prove them wrong.

